<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani rice prices seen steady on low demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistani rice prices seen steady on low demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani rice export prices are likely to remain stable next week amid declining demand from abroad, dealers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Prices were steady this week with exports sluggish, an official at the state-run Rice Export Corp of Pakistan said.</p>
<p>In September rice exports fell to 74,748 tonnes worth $24 million, compared with 97,779 tonnes worth $31 million in August and 72,484 tonnes worth $27 million in September 1995.</p>
<p>Following are exporters FOB rates per tonne:</p>
<p>						 Thurs	 Oct 17</p>
<p>    Basmati				  $500	  $500</p>
<p>    IRRI-6				   $240	  $240</p>
